{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 as the cluster’s restricted internal NTP source and node2 to synchronize exclusively from node1. Both nodes retained RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0, passed sequential restart persistence checks, and are healthy and synchronized.","actions_performed":["Reused the installed chrony 4.6.1 package; no packages, OS release, or kernel were changed.","Configured node1 to serve NTP only to node2 (10.100.85.11/32), enforced by both chrony and persistent firewalld rules.","Configured node2 with node1 (10.100.85.10) as its sole effective time source; public-pool and DHCP-derived sources were disabled.","Preserved the original configuration on each node as /etc/chrony.conf.pre-internal-time with original ownership and permissions.","Restarted node1 and node2 sequentially and verified changed boot identities, service recovery, configuration persistence, synchronization, SELinux enforcement, SSH access, and zero failed units."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Pre-change discovery on both nodes","command_ids":["cmd-b0a4c95be67445f5","cmd-5018e331c1e740ae"],"summary":"Captured RHEL release, kernel, chrony version/configuration, boot IDs, networking, listeners, firewall, checksums, service state, failures, and administrative access."},{"requirement":"Node1 is the restricted internal time source","command_ids":["cmd-0c9528e7d0634d36","cmd-3fdcfe6d8c954a9b","cmd-509300de3f134503"],"summary":"Chrony configuration validates with allow 10.100.85.11/32; UDP/123 is listening; matching runtime and permanent firewalld rules are present; chronyd is active, enabled, and synchronized."},{"requirement":"Node2 synchronizes only against node1 instead of public servers","command_ids":["cmd-4a5799a99b114bad","cmd-09c49d3022584689","cmd-99a47ce81b6c40b0"],"summary":"Effective configuration contains only server 10.100.85.10; node2 automatically selected that source, reports NTPSynchronized=yes, and direct NTP queries succeeded before and after restart."},{"requirement":"Node1 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-6f0099fb73204473","cmd-8dcfa925b2bb40b6","cmd-3aacc1a2df37452b","cmd-e39a99acaed04314","cmd-ba0b324e2c2a439c"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID d49beed9-... was captured; native reboot was acknowledged; boot ID changed to 91621ab0-...; chronyd, listener, firewall restriction, checksum, synchronization, SSH, and node2-to-node1 queries recovered."},{"requirement":"Node2 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-ba0b324e2c2a439c","cmd-a28b6b0a5df948f7","cmd-6551e5bdd5ef4104","cmd-e545a17d971b441f","cmd-99a47ce81b6c40b0"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID d9f8550d-... was captured; native reboot was acknowledged; boot ID changed to eaa42f1f-...; node2 automatically reselected node1 and recovered synchronization, configuration integrity, SSH, and clean service state."},{"requirement":"Operating system, kernel, security controls, and access preserved","command_ids":["cmd-b0a4c95be67445f5","cmd-5018e331c1e740ae","cmd-509300de3f134503","cmd-99a47ce81b6c40b0"],"summary":"Both nodes remain on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 and chrony 4.6.1; SELinux remains enforcing, firewalld remains running, SSH remains available, and no failed units are present."}]}
